+# Narrowing the Veterinarian Directory by Specialty Is In Scope; Free-Text Veterinarian Search Is Not
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian. Like every row but NG-4 and NG-5, it was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey, so whether it was ever decided stayed unknown.
+
+A request then arrived to narrow the veterinarian directory to one specialty. That reads against NG-9 two ways: as the declined veterinarian search, or as a filter on an attribute the directory already prints. The row could not settle which.
+
+The owner decided the row on 2026-08-15, narrowing rather than confirming it.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Confirm NG-9 whole.** Decline the request as veterinarian search. Rejected by the owner: the directory already shows the specialty, so narrowing by it adds no search surface.
+2. **Withdraw NG-9.** Open veterinarian search generally. Rejected: free-text matching across veterinarian names would repeat what owner search already demonstrates.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen): free-text veterinarian search stays out; narrowing the directory by a shown attribute comes in.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 stays a non-goal for free-text search over pets, visits, and veterinarians. It no longer covers narrowing the veterinarian directory to one whole specialty name, which becomes REQ-VET-003.
+
+The boundary is the attribute the directory already publishes. A future request to match on a veterinarian's name, or on a partial specialty, meets NG-9 unnarrowed and needs its own recorded owner decision.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation, joining NG-4 and NG-5 as a decided row. Every other row remains part of it.
+- The machine-readable veterinarian list becomes a supported surface again, so the route no longer sits in the code pending removal.
+- Whether the narrowing gains a visible page control is a separate request, recorded as an open question.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row and the preamble naming it decided.
+- [REQ-VET-003](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the capability the narrowing admits.
